te_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":38918.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1569.0,"requests":4},"prerequisite-consistency":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":6016.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":78.0,"requests":1},"project.measurement-provenance":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":33637.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1031.0,"requests":4},"project.portability":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":2334.75,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":330.5,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":27760.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":985.0,"requests":2}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion (in S3, or a named child) asserting the Git factory preserves its provider-native auth lifecycle, constructs only the selected integration, and fails before network/push on missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth with no anonymous/cross-provider/alternate-principal fallback.","cohort":["G3","G4"],"criteria":["G3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent AC5: 'Git and bridge factories preserve provider-native auth lifecycles and instantiate only the selected integration; missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth fails before network/write without anonymous, cross-provider, or alternate-principal fallback.'","S3 (6e3b) ACs name only DIG/Cloud-write-scope fail-closed and child-env; the Git push auth-lifecycle / fail-before-network outcome appears only in S3 Testing ('Failure-injection tests cover missing project/auth, revoked credential'), not as an AC.","S2 (e042) AC4 covers this outcome for Jira only; S5 (5851) AC3 covers it for review-bot Gerrit/GitHub only — neither exceeds scope to the reconciler/store Git push factory.","container pairing: parent + 5851-51d7-fda8-4966/6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6/6f14-21a7-d806-44b2/a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11/aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4/bbdc-5cc9-097a-4f06/e042-4780-6c63-4b09"],"finding":"Parent AC5's Git half is only partially covered: no child's acceptance criteria assert that the Git factory 'preserves provider-native auth lifecycles', 'instantiates only the selected integration', and that 'missing/conflicting decision-bearing auth fails before network/write without anonymous, cross-provider, or alternate-principal fallback' for Git specifically. S2 (e042) delivers this for the Jira bridge only, and S5 (5851) for review-bot Gerrit/GitHub only. S3 (6e3b) is the child that threads GitRuntime and owns Git adapter/ref/lock/push, but its enumerated ACs cover only (a) apply/Git/delivery paths completing with poisoned resolvers, (b) the Cloud-write/DIG fail-closed case, (c) child-env, (d) no-global-mutation, (e) provider-neutral regression, (f) facade rollback — none states the Git auth-lifecycle-preservation or the fail-before-Git-push-without-alternate-principal outcome as an acceptance criterion. S3 mentions 'revoked credential' only inside a Testing bullet, not as an AC oracle.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f75bfee7f9fe88d68","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child 6e3b-3d1a-0ff7-44b6 (RP-04 S3); cross-checked against child e042 (S2) and child 5851 (S5)","norm_id":"n421d9d6195b28a91","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reconciler Git push with revoked/missing decision-bearing Git credential falls back to an ambient SSH agent identity (alternate principal) and the AC-level completion verifier has no child oracle asserting it must fail-closed first.","Git factory silently re-derives auth from ambient env after composition because no child AC pins 'provider-native auth lifecycle preserved / only selected integration constructed' for Git."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Promote S3's Git failure-injection scenario to an explicit S3 acceptance criterion mirroring S2 AC4 but scoped to GitRuntime/push (fail before network/write, no alternate-principal fallback, only selected integration, lifecycle preserved).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add acceptance criteria that explicitly verify the DIG-scope removal from Jira Cloud writes and that tracker layout reaches every owner, so each named correction has a covering criterion.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Jira Cloud write scope loses `DIG`'","'tracker layout reaches every owner'","No AC line names DIG scope or tracker-layout propagation as a verified outcome"],"finding":"The 'Explicit corrections' list names concrete behavior changes — 'Jira Cloud write scope loses DIG' and 'tracker layout reaches every owner' — that do not map to any acceptance criterion; the ACs cover precedence/root and consumer projections generally but no criterion verifies these specific deltas.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdca1870fc8a27a55","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope > Explicit corrections; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n08a0fdcfd639eea1","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor lands the precedence work but silently leaves DIG in the Jira write scope, or fails to propagate tracker layout to every owner, with no failing criterion"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the bound for live canaries (max requests/cost/time per provider) so 'bounded' is a decision rather than executor discretion.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'bounded live Anthropic/Bedrock cache/auth canaries'","'reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live canaries'","No definition of 'bounded' (count/cost/time)"],"finding":"Multiple ACs and design bullets require 'bounded live' canaries (e.g. 'bounded live Anthropic/Bedrock cache/auth canaries', 'bounded-live canaries') without stating the bound (request count, cost, or time), leaving the executor to guess the limit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f96396b4cf7aeb438","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (LLM cutover bullet; operator-attested bullet)","norm_id":"n5105038bbef98521","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor runs live canaries against Anthropic/Bedrock with no stated ceiling on requests or spend"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a default such as 'bounded = at most N live requests per provider per canary run' to the plan.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docs/config.md: a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11 & aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4 (no ordering edge)"],"finding":"Sibling tickets touch the same file(s) with no ordering edge.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f82524518cbf636a6","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"na0177dc3af65d74f","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a depends_on/blocks edge to serialize, or partition the file ownership.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["9 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[operator-attested] AWS review-bot and reconciler check/dry-run/bounded-live can' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the epic-spanning ACs are decomposed into the vertical children (each with its own in-session-verifiable oracle) before this epic is claimed, and reference those children from the ACs.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T4"],"criteria":["F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Every affected consumer receives an immutable projection/runtime binding and no in-progress operation rereads ambient state.'","Sequencing: 'Create and link vertical implementation children with behavioral oracles and exact file impact before reviewing or claiming this epic.'"],"finding":"Several acceptance criteria span the full set of subsystems (LLM, Git, bridge, MCP, op-cert, review-bot, reconciler, docs) as one epic-of-epics without per-child right-sizing; e.g. 'Every affected consumer receives an immutable projection/runtime binding' aggregates all CLI/library/MCP/reconciler/hosted consumers into a single check, so the criterion is not in-session completable as a coherent single-outcome deliverable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f71563e5e23f8273d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (2nd bullet) and Sequencing","norm_id":"n5548fcaa7118c412","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer cannot complete or evaluate the epic-level AC in one session because it depends on many separate subsystem cutovers"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation